  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> be the relation defined on the set of all real numbers such that <math> <mrow> <mtext>P</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>a,&#160;b</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> <mtext>&#160;:&#160;</mtext> <msup> <mtext>sec</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mtext>a</mtext><mo>-</mo> <msup> <mtext>tan</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mtext>b</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </math>. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> is&nbsp;</p>\r"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "reflexive and symmetric but not transitive",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "symmetric and transitive but not reflexive",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "reflexive and transitive but not symmetric",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "an equivalence relation",
      "is_correct": true
